g the 2026-09-04 backfill had stored and quarantined for recogniser damage was not used. Every word was then read on the 1862 Pustet at printed pp. 448-449, Festa Maji (25), S. Gregorii VII, Oratio (turning the page at tuenda / Ecclesiae), read on the page image of its registered facsimile PDF at pp. 534-535 (text-layer address lines 63345-63348 and 63359-63363), which carries the text word for word. Differences from the antecedent: the 1862 sets no comma after Deus and sets one after tuum.","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-10-01 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.s-gregorii-vii-papae-confessoris-collect","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 534, no. 2638, marked P; artifact PDF p. 615, foot of the right column, under 'Die 25 maii, S. Gregorii VII Papae et Conf.'","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-s-gregorii-vii-papae-confessoris-orations"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"The wording is preexisting material of the 1962 typical edition under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), which gives a revised edition no exclusive right in material it did not contribute. The independent registered public-domain witness is the tracked 1862 Pustet text artifact and its registered facsimile PDF, read on a page image. The position is settled for the repository at src/sources/inventories/missale-romanum-1962-facsimile-rights-v1.toml, which requires exactly this pairing of 103(b) with a public-domain witness.","locator":"Pustet Ratisbon 1862, Festa Maji (25), S. Gregorii VII, Oratio (turning the page at tuenda / Ecclesiae), printed pp. 448-449; text-layer lines 63345-63348 and 63359-63363; read on the page image of the registered facsimile PDF at pp. 534-535; artifact rights_status public-domain on a book first published in 1862","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.ki054-page-reading-orations-7d558094","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.missale-romanum-1862-text-f34bc7cf","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.ia-facsimile-pdf-363d6fc3"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"947e32b2589ddea2b3c65fd46d1e35043752d058bf73445396d7d5d0ef78f5e5","withheld":false},"name":"Collect","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Deus, in te sperantium fortitudo, qui beatum Gregorium Confessorem tuum\natque Pontificem, pro tuenda Ecclesiae libertate, virtute constantiae\nroborasti: da nobis, ejus exemplo et intercessione, omnia adversantia\nfortiter superare. Per Dominum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"A lay hand missal of the 1945 revision, printed about 1955-56, not an approved liturgical translation and never an altar book. Its Holy Week is the pre-1955 rite, its sanctoral is not the 1962 sanctoral, and its second and third orations are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nLeaf n1017, printed p. 1025, under `Prayer` in the Mass of St Gregory VII. The page prints the complete facing Latin and English with Gregory's name, so no saint-name substitution or wording is supplied by this inventory.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.francis-xavier-lasance.the-new-roman-missal.benziger-revised-1945","source_label":"The New Roman Missal in Latin and English, revised edition, by F. X. Lasance and Francis Augustine Walsh (New York: Benziger Brothers, 1945), ca. 1955-56 printing (Internet Archive delivery locator fr-lasance-missal-1937; locator mislabelled)","text":"O God, the strength of them that trust in Thee, Who didst fortify blessed Gregory, Thy Confessor and Pontiff, with the virtue of constancy, for the defense of the liberty of the Church, grant us by his example and intercession courageously to overcome all adversities. Through our Lord.\n"}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"1 Peter","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":5,"first":1,"last":4}]},"ref":"1 Peter 5:1-4","token":"1Pet","unresolved":null},{"book":"1 Peter","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":5,"first":10,"last":11}]},"ref":"1 Peter 5:10-11","token":"1Pet","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]},{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"en","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]}],"occurrence_id":"roman-1962%3As-gregorii-vii-papae-confessoris%3Amain%3A3:all:all","schema":"triptych-missal-unit-coverage/v1","target_id":"roman-1962%3Aproper%3Acommune-summorum-pontificum%3Amain%3AEpistle%3A1:all:all"},"cycles":{},"form":"","form_id":"main","incipit":null,"languages":[{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"la","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"},{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"en","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"}],"latin":null,"name":"Epistle","source":"scripture","taken_from":{"citation":"Commune unius aut plurium Summorum